    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{5\\pi}{4}$.",
      "worked": "The original expression requires $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\cos^3\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}+\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\n&=\\frac{\\cos\\theta(\\cos^2\\theta+\\sin^2\\theta)}{\\sin\\theta}\\\\\n\\frac{\\cos^3\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}+\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\n&=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nHence\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}&=1\\\\\n\\cos\\theta&=\\sin\\theta\\\\\n\\tan\\theta&=1\\\\\n\\theta&=\\frac{\\pi}{4},\\frac{5\\pi}{4}.\n\\end{align*}$$\nBoth values lie in $[0,2\\pi]$ and have nonzero sine.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
